            <ArticleTitle>Eagle syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>201-202</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.806</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although rare, Eagle syndrome should be always considered in the differential diagnosis in patients with chronic orofacial pain refractory to conventional treatments. Treatment is surgery and exeresis of the styloid process via a transoral or cervical approach depending on clinical and radiological features.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
